  <data name="About_Tagline.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A study project on screen sharing.</value></data>
  <data name="About_Description.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Beamcast is a lab: it captures a Windows screen or window straight on the GPU, compresses it with the hardware H.264 or HEVC encoder (VP8 on the CPU as a fallback) and streams it over TCP to anyone holding the invite code. It exists to study codecs, capture and real-time streaming, and as a case study for a separate enterprise application.</value></data>
  <data name="About_Version" xml:space="preserve"><value>Version {0}</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardShareTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Broadcast</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardShareBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Pick a screen or window, tune the quality and go live. Capture stays on the GPU and the hardware encoder (H.264/HEVC) compresses it before it goes over TCP.</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardJoinTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Watch</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardJoinBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Paste the code, join and watch. Double-click for fullscreen.</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardNetTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Network</value></data>
  <data name="About_CardNetBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Works out of the box on the same network. Over the internet, the broadcaster needs to forward the port on the router.</value></data>

  <data name="Title_StudyBadge.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>STUDY PROJECT</value></data>

  <data name="Disclaimer_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Before you use it: this is a study project</value></data>
  <data name="Disclaimer_Heading.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Study project. Read before use.</value></data>
  <data name="Disclaimer_P1" xml:space="preserve"><value>Beamcast exists only for study and case studies about screen capture, video codecs and real-time streaming on Windows. It is the research base for a separate, private, enterprise application. It is not a product and was not built for real use.</value></data>
  <data name="Disclaimer_P2" xml:space="preserve"><value>Any use of this app or this code for other purposes is the sole responsibility of whoever uses it. By using it you declare that you are aware of this and accept every risk, including exposing whatever is on your screen.</value></data>
  <data name="Disclaimer_P3" xml:space="preserve"><value>The author accepts no responsibility for the use, the results, losses or damages arising from this software. It is provided "as is", with no warranty, no support and no maintenance commitment.</value></data>
  <data name="Disclaimer_P4" xml:space="preserve"><value>The app has not been hardened for production. Video is end-to-end encrypted, but use it only in study environments you control.</value></data>
  <data name="Disclaimer_P1_Text.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Beamcast exists only for study and case studies about screen capture, video codecs and real-time streaming on Windows. It is the research base for a separate, private, enterprise application. It is not a product and was not built for real use.</value></data>
