  <data name="Nav_Lounge.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Lounge</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Heading.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Lounge</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Summary.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Point at the server of whoever hosts Beamcast, create a lounge with a password or join one with its code. Inside, anyone can broadcast their screen and everyone picks what to watch.</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Server.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Server (host or IP)</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Server.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve"><value>192.168.1.20 or wss://beamcast.example.com</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_YourName.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Your name</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_CreateHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Create a lounge</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_CreateHint.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The password is required: it becomes the key that encrypts everything end to end. The server never receives it.</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Name.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Lounge name</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Name.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve"><value>e.g. Friends' room</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_CreatePassword.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Password (min. 4 characters)</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_CreateButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Create lounge</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_JoinHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Join a lounge</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_JoinHint.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Paste the code (or the BC-… invite) you were given and the lounge password.</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Code.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Code or invite</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_Code.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve"><value>ABC234 or BC-…</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_JoinPassword.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Lounge password</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_JoinButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Join</value></data>
  <data name="Lounge_SecurityNote.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Everything that flows through the lounge (names, titles, video and audio) is encrypted with AES-256-GCM under a key derived from the password. The server only sees ciphertext and a password proof; it cannot watch or listen.</value></data>
